A||||9||Jaei Sun||Test Drove a 2.8 5-speed!||||10||
Z||000000||Jaei Sun||07-28-2000||02:02 AM||||What a blast!!! I fell in love with it right away... like a big go-cart but hella better.  Now I'm trying to find financing to purchase it. Tho it had 2 problems with it. The first was a clicking sound coming from the engine compartment while the engine was idling and running.  And there seemed to have oil leaking from the distrib. cap... Anyone know what might be causing these?? The engine only has 61k miles on it too!!! BONUS!||||reg||10
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-28-2000||02:44 AM||||Easy...the "clicking" noise from the engine is more than likey and exhaust leak (Id hope that it was from the rear exhaust manifold, the front one is a PAIN to change)....could be lifters taping, but more than likey its an exhaust leak. Keep in mind there is supposed to be a very subtle "ticking" type sound, thats the injectors doing there job.<BR>The oil leak from around the distributor is the distributor O-ring. Pretty easy fix, pull the dist and replace the O-ring! Pontiac dealerships still carry these, around 50 cents. Remember to mark the position, so that setting the timming will be easy upon re-installation. Id actually go on and replace the pickup coil and ignition module while you got the thing out! <BR>Drive on!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-28-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||Standard||07-28-2000||02:50 AM||||Wonderful, isn't it?<P>The clicking was most likely a crack in the front(firewall) manifold.. it's very common and it's a pain to get at... And the leak is the O-ring, just like My7 said.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||07-28-2000||12:55 PM||||Just hope and pray the bolt heads on the manifold aren't broken off. If they are, like on mine, you better get some Advil! LOL  If you need help any step of the way, let us know. I'm sure there are hundreds on the forum that have had the same problems on their Fiero (s). <P>Get the Fiero!! You'll love it!!!  Don't forget to post pics!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||07-28-2000||02:10 PM||||Make sure the clicking isn't just the injectors switching first.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jaei Sun||07-28-2000||05:23 PM||||WOW thanks for all the info I'll give the engine a closer look when I get another chance to look at it... Probably when I'm giving the guy the check  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000006||88formula||07-28-2000||08:53 PM||||There is nothing like a stick in a mid-engine sports car! I felt the same way you do now about the five speed manual transmission when I first test drove the formula I have now. I can still remember the time I first heard the rumble of the exhaust as the owner backed it out his garage, it mad an impression on me.<P>The ticking noise is most likely a leaking exhaust manifold. It happened to my formula when the previous owner had it and then six months after I bought it. It gives you an excuse to port the manifolds out which is good for 8-horsepower. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||07-29-2000||12:07 AM||||Terry is right, all MPFI V6's have a distinct click.  But if it sounds like a ffft-ffft-ffft it's an exhaust leak. Sometimes it IS difficult to tell the difference if the exhaust leak is in the early stages. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Jaei Sun||07-29-2000||05:55 AM||||I'm heading out there Sun. to really examine it.. (it is located an hour away from me)<p>[This message has been edited by Jaei Sun (edited 07-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||07-29-2000||07:09 PM||||Jaei Sun...<P>Take about a five foot piece of garden hose with you. Use it like a stethoscope to poke around the engine compartment while it's running. (Watch out for the pulleys.) If the ticking is coming from under the orange intake plenum, it's probably only the injectors. <BR>Good luck!<BR><P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
